# Cloudflare Pages caching rules.
#
# Without these, Pages serves everything as `max-age=0, must-revalidate`, so a
# returning visitor revalidates all 33 village models before the scene can
# start — 33 round trips to be told nothing changed.
#
# Astro hashes its own filenames, so those can be cached forever. The models
# live at stable paths and carry a ?v= stamp instead (see village-models.ts),
# so they get a week, with revalidation after that as a backstop in case the
# stamp is ever forgotten.

# HTML must never be cached: it names the hashed assets, and a stale copy asks
# for files a later deploy has already removed.
/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800
